# Lifecycle: creation defaults, reference counting, deferred destruction.
# A source is destroyed when its LAST strong reference is released, but the destroy callback, the "destroy"
# signal and the memory release are deferred to a task queue ("drain").  Names are not freed until then.
kind in input video create,destroy,update,defaults
watch_global
create a in A
watch a
info a
get_setting a dflt
refs a
addref a
refs a
release a
refs a
release a
pending
echo before-drain
drain
pending
